{
  "version": 1,
  "language": "italian",
  "chapter": 36,
  "title": "Reading — Words, Lines, and a First Passage",
  "drivablePrefix": 2,
  "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:b0893f4f68f8b0ca",
  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "IT-C36-parole",
      "sequence": 1380,
      "title": "(reading) — six words off a counter",
      "headword": "(reading)",
      "romanization": "(reading)",
      "gloss": "six words read cold — and the article that comes with every one of them",
      "script": "latin",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:b4a978ada57decf2",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Every word below you have met. Not one is new."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What is new is that nobody says them first."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "comprehension",
          "title": "Reading",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "caffè pane acqua libro amico casa."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Read down the list once, without stopping."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Again — and notice that on a real sign each of these would arrive with a word in front of it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "culture-pragmatics",
          "title": "Why it's said this way",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Italian almost never writes a noun bare. Il libro, l'acqua, un caffè — the article is part of how the word arrives."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "That is why a list like this one is slightly unusual to an Italian eye, and why a menu is easier to read than it looks: the article in front tells you the gender before you have to remember it."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Six words, and each one is a decision the page will normally make for you."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "the six words down the list, once, without stopping",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: the six words down the list, once, without stopping]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "repeat",
              "times": 2,
              "source": "[REPEAT x2]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "activity",
              "scored": true,
              "id": "IT-C36-parole-water",
              "prompt": "Which word is water?",
              "assesses": [
                "IT-SKILL-READ-WORDS"
              ],
              "responseSeconds": 12,
              "acceptedResponses": [
                "acqua",
                "l'acqua",
                "water"
              ],
              "feedback": {
                "correct": "acqua.",
                "incorrect": "acqua -- water."
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "How many of the six were new? (None.)"
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What would normally stand in front of each one? (An article — and it carries the gender.)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "IT-C36-frasi",
      "sequence": 1390,
      "title": "(reading) — six lines, three of them one word",
      "headword": "(reading)",
      "romanization": "(reading)",
      "gloss": "six lines you would say at a counter — three of them one word",
      "script": "latin",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:1174c373e15363dc",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The last lesson gave you words. These are things you would say."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "You have said every one of them."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "comprehension",
          "title": "Reading",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Ciao! Grazie! Arrivederci! Non so. Che buono! Questo è Marco."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Read down once, without stopping."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Again — and notice the list gets longer as it goes, from one word to three."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "culture-pragmatics",
          "title": "Why it's said this way",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Non so is two words and a complete sentence. Italian puts the person in the verb, so so is already I know, and non in front of it is the whole negative."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Arrivederci is the longest line here and the easiest to recognise, because length and difficulty are not the same thing on a page. You meet that word as a shape long before you take it apart."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Six lines, and the shortest one is the one that needs a verb."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "the six lines, once, in order, without stopping",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: the six lines, once, in order, without stopping]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "repeat",
              "times": 2,
              "source": "[REPEAT x2]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "activity",
              "scored": true,
              "id": "IT-C36-frasi-dontknow",
              "prompt": "Which line says you do not know?",
              "assesses": [
                "IT-SKILL-READ-LINES"
              ],
              "responseSeconds": 12,
              "acceptedResponses": [
                "non so",
                "non so.",
                "i don't know"
              ],
              "feedback": {
                "correct": "Non so.",
                "incorrect": "Non so -- I don't know."
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "How many of the six were new? (None.)"
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Where is the I in Non so? (Inside the verb.)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "IT-C36-prima-lettura",
      "sequence": 1400,
      "title": "(reading) — the first passage",
      "headword": "(reading)",
      "romanization": "(reading)",
      "gloss": "the first passage — forty-seven words of Italian in a row, and not one of them new",
      "script": "latin",
      "modality": "sight",
      "derivedModality": "sight",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "sight-cue"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:941579d00f4bef60",
      "notice": {
        "modality": "sight",
        "needs": [
          "your eyes, because the lesson points at something written down"
        ],
        "waitUntilStopped": [],
        "text": "Before we start: this one needs your eyes, so it is not fully a driving lesson. You will want your eyes, because the lesson points at something written down. You can listen to all of it now and come back to the parts that need looking at once you have stopped."
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Six words, then six lines. Now twelve of them together."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Forty-seven words, and not one of them is new."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "comprehension",
          "title": "Reading",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Ciao! Il mio nome è Marco. Questo è il mio amico. Lui è molto buono. Oggi ho un caffè. Ho anche il pane. Leggo un libro, ma non capisco. Non so perché. Il libro è abbastanza buono. Qui c'è l'acqua. Domani leggo il libro. Grazie e arrivederci!"
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Read it once without stopping. Do not translate as you go — let the sentences arrive."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Now read it again, and look at the word perché."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "culture-pragmatics",
          "title": "Why it's said this way",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Perché is both why and because. Italian does not give you two words for those, so a reader decides which one from where it sits."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Here it sits after Non so, so it is why. Had it opened a clause after a full sentence, it would have been because. You have done a piece of reading with no equivalent in English, and nothing on the page marked it."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Notice also il mio nome. Italian keeps the article in front of the possessive, which Spanish does not, and it is the kind of small difference that only becomes visible when you read rather than translate."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "This is the first whole passage the book has asked you to hold at once, and it works because everything in it was paid for."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "the passage aloud, once, without stopping",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: the passage aloud, once, without stopping]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "repeat",
              "times": 2,
              "source": "[REPEAT x2]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "activity",
              "scored": true,
              "id": "IT-C36-prima-lettura-perche",
              "prompt": "In this passage, does perché mean why or because?",
              "assesses": [
                "IT-SKILL-CONNECTED-READING"
              ],
              "responseSeconds": 14,
              "acceptedResponses": [
                "why",
                "perché = why"
              ],
              "feedback": {
                "correct": "Why -- it follows Non so.",
                "incorrect": "Why. It follows Non so, so it is the question word."
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "How many words in that passage were new? (None.)"
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What tells you whether perché is asking or answering? (Where it sits — nothing else does.)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "findings": []
}
